# Prod log grep format (Ashutosh)

When sharing **prod** log search commands, use this layout. Change the node list only when Ashutosh says so.

## Box

Central log host. Cwd does not matter if paths are absolute.

- Host example: `ip-10-196-134-114`
- Root: `/apps/applogs`
- Nodes (current): `10.196.134.101` `10.196.134.176` `10.196.134.177` `10.196.134.103` `10.196.134.74` `10.196.134.80`

## Do

- `grep` (never `rg`). One-liners. `# N purpose` above each command. One fenced `bash` block.
- Brace all six nodes and `{dsa,common}` (or the tenant in play).
- Live and archived as **separate** commands. `zgrep` for `.gz`.
- Live: `/apps/applogs/10.196.134.{101,176,177,103,74,80}/{dsa,common}/{service}-{tenant}.log`
- Archived: `/apps/applogs/10.196.134.{101,176,177,103,74,80}/{dsa,common}/archived/archived-logs-YYYY-MM/{service}/YYYY-MM-DD-{service}-{tenant}*.log.gz`

```bash
# 1 Prod live
grep -a 'STAN' /apps/applogs/10.196.134.{101,176,177,103,74,80}/{dsa,common}/credit-card-management-dsa.log 2>/dev/null | grep -a 'executeInterfaceService'

# 2 Prod archived that calendar day
zgrep -a 'STAN' /apps/applogs/10.196.134.{101,176,177,103,74,80}/{dsa,common}/archived/archived-logs-2026-10/credit-card-management/2026-10-05-credit-card-management-dsa*.log.gz 2>/dev/null | grep -a 'executeInterfaceService'
```

## Do not

- Do not use `/apps/applogs/dsa/` or `/apps/applogs/common/` with **no node IP** for prod.
- Do not mix live `.log` and archived `.gz` in one command.
- QA/UAT stay `/apps/applogs/{common|tenant}/` unless Ashutosh shows a node-prefixed tree there too.
